{"id": "q_the_emergency_council_meeting_1", "question": "What are the wizards asking the council to do in the emergency meeting-and what's the catch?", "answer": "TL;DR: The wizards are pushing for a city-wide magical purification/detection sweep, but the catch is it affects the entire population and may require lockdowns or sealing parts of the city, risking panic, isolation, and collateral harm.\n\nFrom the available facts, the Wizard’s College (referenced alongside Tinkerbright as actively detecting the cult) is tied to proposals that the city is “subject of a proposed city-wide purification effort” and that it “requires purification of the entire city” (CANON: the city operational_status, physical_condition). This strongly indicates they want sweeping magical action to expose or eliminate cult influence—likely leveraging the fact that “cultists can be immediately detected by magic” (CANON: the cult operational_status).\n\nThe catch is embedded in the same cluster of consequences:\n- A “city-wide lockdown is being pushed for” (CANON: the city operational_status)\n- “Parts of the city could be left isolated if key tunnels or access points are sealed” (CANON)\n- The city risks being “brought closer to disaster by each failed or unresolved debate” (CANON)\n\nSo while effective against the cult, the plan risks mass disruption, harming or targeting ordinary citizens, and potentially accelerating chaos the cult can exploit.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Defenses: Magical detection can identify cultists\n- Operational Status: Proposed city-wide purification; lockdown pressure; risk of isolation\n- Conflict: Active cult threat beneath the city; coordinated attacks ongoing\n- Governance: Council under time pressure, divided on action", "has_error": false, "retrieval": {"enabled": true, "top_k": 30, "pre_filter_count": 2069, "post_filter_count": 30, "duration_ms": 83, "top_5": [["ent_council", 2.46], ["ent_wizards", 1.9005], ["ent_step_2_discussion_rounds", 1.4116], ["ent_wizards_