{"id": "q_pre_post", "question": "Before vs after the council fight-how's the Wolf different?", "answer": "TL;DR: Before the council fight, The Wolf is an active saboteur stalling and manipulating inside the chamber; after it, he’s a fleeing, wounded escapee who successfully slipped into the sewers and shifted into pursuit/ritual-phase play.\n\n**Before the council fight (OBSERVED):**  \n- **Location:** In the council chamber during the encounter.  \n- **Role/Behavior:** مباشر disruption—creates confusion, delays players, and pressures the council situation.  \n- **Tactics:** Heavy use of illusion and misdirection (illusory duplicates, large-scale distractions).  \n- **Goal:** Reach the **secret escape tunnel beneath the council chamber** while stalling the party.  \n- **State:** Engaged but cautious—plans to disengage once pressured.\n\n**After the council fight (OBSERVED):**  \n- **Location:** Escaped via **secret passage** into the **sewers**; later part of a chase sequence and tied to a **ritual chamber**.  \n- **Role/Behavior:** No longer holding ground—now evading and progressing the larger cult plan.  \n- **Tactics Shift:** Triggers **invisibility when below 50% HP**, uses a **massive illusion** to cover escape.  \n- **Goal:** Continue toward the **kaiju summoning ritual** and regroup.  \n- **State:** Successfully escaped, transitioning from encounter boss → ongoing threat.\n\n**Key Attributes:**  \n- **Faction:** Cultist  \n- **Rank/Title:** Second in command of the guard  \n- **Core Tactics:** Illusion, invisibility, delay → escape  \n- **Arc Shift:** Saboteur in control → wounded escapee advancing the next phase", "has_error": false, "retrieval": {"enabled": true, "top_k": 30, "pre_filter_count": 2069, "post_filter_count": 30, "duration_ms": 60, "top_5": [["ent_the_wolf", 1.9365], ["ent_council", 1.66], ["ent_secret_escape_tunnel", 1.6294], ["ent_a_broken_sword", 1.4818], ["ent_eirik", 1.4565]], "selected_entity_ids": ["ent_the_wolf", "ent_council", "ent_s